  "answer": "Yes. NovaLearn should fund the Advanced OCR Pipeline before accelerating the Microsoft Teams integration.\n\n- **Current support demand:** Scanned PDF imports and broken citations drove 27% of support tickets in May [NL-015], and scanned policy documents are the primary driver of citation errors and customer onboarding delays [NL-001]. The Advanced OCR Pipeline is therefore the highest technical priority, scheduled for August 2026 [NL-001].\n- **Onboarding impact:** Scanned PDF ingestion remains the primary onboarding bottleneck, and resolving citation reliability is critical for regulated customers [NL-016]. Deferring OCR would keep onboarding delays and support load unresolved.\n- **Roadmap status:** Teams is only in the design phase for Q4 2026 [NL-001][NL-014], with development slated for early 2027 [NL-015]. It is not generally available [NL-023], and rushing it risks a tenant-isolation breach because it requires a redesign of the auth layer to enforce RBAC [NL-015].\n\nGiven these factors, funding OCR first is the right recommendation; Teams acceleration should not come before addressing the ingestion and citation foundation.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
